/* en-it Compliments deck (added later, writer C). One card per line: target | pron | meaning | note. pron generated by tools/target/it/respell.js. */
module.exports = {
  "Compliments": `
Era tutto buonissimo. | EH-rah TOOT-toh bwoh-NEES-see-moh | Everything was delicious. | Say it to the host or cook after a meal; fine with tu or Lei.
Cucini benissimo! | koo-CHEE-nee beh-NEES-see-moh | You're a great cook! | tu form. To someone you call Lei: Cucina benissimo!
Complimenti! | kohm-plee-MEHN-tee | Well done! | For a result, a meal, a new home: to anyone, tu or Lei. It never changes.
Sei bravissimo! | say brah-VEES-see-moh | You're really good at this! | To a woman: Sei bravissima! To someone you call Lei: È bravissimo / bravissima!
Ottima idea! | OHT-tee-mah ee-DEH-ah | Great idea! | ottima agrees with idea (feminine). Fine with anyone.
Sei molto gentile. | say MOHL-toh jehn-TEE-leh | You're very kind. | gentile is the same for men and women. To someone you call Lei: Lei è molto gentile.
Sei proprio divertente! | say PROH-pryoh dee-vehr-TEHN-teh | You're so much fun! | divertente is the same for men and women: funny and fun to be with.
Sei un gran lavoratore. | say oon grahn lah-voh-rah-TOH-reh | You're a really hard worker. | To a woman: Sei una gran lavoratrice. A real compliment in Italy, at work or at home.
Che bella casa! | keh BEHL-lah KAH-sah | What a lovely home! | bella agrees with casa. Works with tu or Lei: no verb.
Ti sta benissimo! | tee stah beh-NEES-see-moh | That looks great on you! | About clothes. To someone you call Lei: Le sta benissimo!
Che bella foto! | keh BEHL-lah FOH-toh | What a nice photo! | foto is feminine (short for fotografia), so bella, not bello.
Parla molto bene l'italiano. | PAHR-lah MOHL-toh BEH-neh lee-tah-LYAH-noh | You speak Italian very well. | What a stranger will say to you, in the Lei form. A friend says: Parli molto bene l'italiano.
Grazie, troppo gentile! | GRAH-tsyeh TROHP-poh jehn-TEE-leh | Thanks, that's so kind of you! | The usual reply in Italy: thank the person warmly. Same with tu or Lei.
Grazie, ma ho ancora tanto da imparare. | GRAH-tsyeh mah oh ahn-KOH-rah TAHN-toh dah eem-pah-RAH-reh | Thanks, but I still have a lot to learn. | A modest reply to praise of your Italian; a little modesty is normal in Italy.
`,
};
